    id: "aifordevs-tool-calling-loop",
    category: "aifordevs",
    difficulty: "Intermediate",
    topic: "Function/Tool Calling",
    title: "How do you implement the agentic loop for multi-step tool calling?",
    summary: "Repeatedly call the model, execute any requested tools, feed results back, and stop when the model returns a final answer.",
    explanation: "A single tool call is often not enough — the model may need to call several tools in sequence, using the result of one to decide the next. The pattern is a loop: send the conversation to the model; if the stop reason indicates a tool call, execute the requested tool(s), append the tool result(s) as a new message, and call the model again; repeat until the model returns a normal text response. You need a hard iteration cap to avoid infinite loops, and you should log each tool call for debugging and auditing since the model's tool choices are not fully deterministic.",
    code: "async function runAgentLoop(initialMessages, tools, maxSteps = 6) {\n  let messages = initialMessages;\n  for (let i = 0; i < maxSteps; i++) {\n    const response = await client.messages.create({\n      model: \"claude-opus-4-8\", max_tokens: 1024, tools, messages,\n    });\n    if (response.stop_reason !== \"tool_use\") {\n      return response.content.find((b) => b.type === \"text\").text;\n    }\n    messages = [...messages, { role: \"assistant\", content: response.content }];\n    const toolResults = [];\n    for (const block of response.content) {\n      if (block.type === \"tool_use\") {\n        const result = await executeTool(block.name, block.input);\n        toolResults.push({ type: \"tool_result\", tool_use_id: block.id, content: result });\n      }\n    }\n    messages = [...messages, { role: \"user\", content: toolResults }];\n  }\n  throw new Error(\"Max tool-calling steps exceeded\");\n}",
    interviewQuestion: "Your agent loop occasionally calls the same tool over and over without making progress. How would you detect and prevent that in production?",
