    explanation: "When a model emits several tool_use blocks in one assistant turn, the API expects every corresponding tool_result to be returned together in a single subsequent user message, matched by tool_use_id. If you only execute and return one of several requested tools, or split results into separate messages, most providers will reject the request or the model will get confused about which result belongs to which call. A common tricky bug is executing tools concurrently with Promise.all but then not preserving the tool_use_id association, causing results to be mismatched i, especially when one tool call fails and you need to return an is_error result rather than skip it entirely.",
