    summary: "A database optimized for storing high-dimensional vectors and performing fast approximate nearest-neighbor similarity search over them.",
    explanation: "Traditional databases index data for exact-match or range queries (B-trees, hash indexes), but similarity search over embeddings requires finding the 'closest' vectors in high-dimensional space, which exact search can't do efficiently at scale. Vector databases (Pinecone, Weaviate, Qdrant, Milvus, or pgvector as a Postgres extension) use approximate nearest neighbor (ANN) algorithms like HNSW to make this fast even with millions of vectors, trading a small amount of accuracy for large speed gains. Most also support storing metadata alongside vectors so you can filter results (e.g. only search within a specific user's documents) in the same query.",
